      "title": "Definitions",
      "type": "text",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The target is **99.9999 %** for each service level. The error budget is the 0.0001 % of failures that the target allows.\n\n- **Colors:** in the stat panels, green is at or above the target. Yellow is at or above 99.99 % and below the target. Red is below 99.99 %.\n- **Probe and submit counts:** the budget is 1 failure in 1,000,000. The canary runs fewer than 1,000,000 probes in 30 days. One failure in 30 days gives 99.99988 %, and an error budget left of -24 %. For a range shorter than about 37 days, read canary success as: 100 %, or a miss. Submit success shows the target only when the range holds 1,000,000 submits or more.\n- **Minute levels** (chain liveness, ingress reachable): the budget is about 2.6 s of downtime in 30 days. These levels count whole minutes at a 1-minute resolution, so they cannot show 2.6 s. One bad minute in 30 days gives 99.998 %. Read them as: 100 %, or a miss.\n\n- **Canary success:** the end-to-end view. A probe passes when its transaction lands with the expected receipt, or its read returns the expected value.\n- **Submit success:** the front-door view. It counts the refusals for `internal`, `timeout`, `overloaded`, `paused` and `draining`.\n- **Chain liveness:** the minutes in which the executed head moved. An idle chain still moves: the sealer closes empty blocks.\n- **Ingress reachable:** the minutes in which at least one ingress answered the scrape."
      }
    }
